UAT Challenges & Validation Dependencies
________________________________________
1. Overview
The production-ready solution was handed over to the RCDP team on 17 July 2026 for UAT testing, with the target production go-live planned for the third week of September 2026.
The solution was developed and validated using Production data and Production reference data, including the Legal Entity and LoB mappings maintained in the Helios Entity Mapper.
During UAT, differences were identified between the Production reference data used by the solution and the corresponding reference data available in the UAT environment. This resulted in discrepancies while validating the Legal Entity and LoB recommendations generated by the solution.
________________________________________
2. Key Challenge
Production vs. UAT Reference Data Mismatch
The solution relies on Production-aligned reference data for contextualization and recommendation generation.
During UAT validation, the RCDP team identified that the LoB and Legal Entity keys generated in the Analytics output were not matching the corresponding keys in the UAT Entity Mapper reference data.
The issue was subsequently clarified as a difference between the Production and UAT reference datasets, rather than an issue with the recommendation-generation process itself.
Impact:
•	Generated recommendations could not be directly reconciled against UAT reference data. 
•	End-to-end validation of the recommendations was impacted. 
•	Additional comparison between Production-aligned and UAT reference data was required. 
•	Data extraction/access restrictions introduced an additional dependency for completing the validation. 
