4. Data Access & Validation Constraints
To perform a like-for-like comparison and validate the observed discrepancies, the team explored obtaining the relevant reference data from the UAT/Production environments.
The following constraints were identified:
•	UAT data could not be freely downloaded to a local environment. 
•	Extraction of data from the CMLP Production environment requires exceptional approval. 
•	Reference data could not be exposed through application/log outputs due to data-handling restrictions. 
•	A full Production-vs-UAT comparison was therefore not immediately feasible. 
•	Targeted comparison using specific alert/case IDs was discussed as an interim validation approach. 
•	Extraction of the relevant Entity Mapper / mapping file from the GCS location was identified as a key dependency. 
________________________________________
5. Agreed Mitigation / Next Steps
1.	Obtain the relevant Entity Mapper / mapping file from the appropriate GCS location. 
2.	Reconcile the Production and UAT reference datasets to establish the exact source of the key discrepancies. 
3.	Perform targeted validation using specific alert/case IDs where a complete dataset comparison is not feasible. 
4.	Initiate the required approval process for any necessary Production data extraction. 
5.	Complete validation of the Analytics recommendations against the appropriate Production-aligned reference data. 
6.	Confirm whether any solution changes are required following completion of the reconciliation. 
7.	Track closure of the above dependency prior to production deployment. 
________________________________________
6. Project Impact
The solution code was production-ready and handed over on 17 July 2026. The subsequent UAT validation challenge arose from the difference in reference data between the UAT and Production environments.
As a result, additional data reconciliation and access/approval activities became necessary to establish a like-for-like validation baseline.
Given the planned third-week-of-September go-live, this dependency became a critical item for completing UAT validation and obtaining the required confidence/sign-off for production deployment.
